## Frozen P8 policy

P8 accumulates source statistics only while the ordinary source DAG is constructed. It performs no separate dispatch traversal. A frozen depth-3 regression tree predicts P6/direct compiler-pipeline cost and dispatches to P6 only when the predicted ratio is at most the frozen cutoff.

Training/validation were disjoint from the 36 Gate-P evaluation cases and from the ten frozen EPFL evaluation roots.

- training cases: 188
- validation cases: 98
- selected cutoff: `0.80`
- tree features actually used: `binary_density`, `max_depth`, `max_pair_shells`, `pair_repeat_density`, `reuse_density`
- selected validation source-inclusive geomean ratio: `1.223847`
- selected validation workload-weighted ratio: `1.063285`
- validation annotated cases: 4

The cutoff was selected by the preregistered conservative tie rule and was not retuned after evaluation.

## Gate-P primary: source-inclusive

Primary endpoint includes source-DAG construction, compiler DAG construction, and sparse-ANF lowering.

| Comparison | Case-balanced geomean | 95% bootstrap CI | Workload-weighted | Wins |
|---|---:|---:|---:|---:|
| P8 / direct | **1.141292** | **1.062175-1.196624** | **1.102416** | 2/36 |
| P8 / always-P6 | 1.071587 | 1.029307-1.119132 | 1.083592 | 9/36 |
| always-P6 / direct | 1.065049 | 0.978723-1.141712 | 1.017371 | 7/36 |

Therefore P8 is about 14.1% slower than direct case-balanced and 10.2% slower workload-weighted on the preregistered primary endpoint. The predeclared source-inclusive PASS criterion is `false`.

## Gate-P secondary: compiler-only

This endpoint starts from an already-built telemetry-compatible source root. It isolates the frozen dispatch decision plus the selected compiler backend from the telemetry-construction tax.

| Comparison | Case-balanced geomean | 95% bootstrap CI | Workload-weighted | Wins |
|---|---:|---:|---:|---:|
| P8 / direct | **0.976949** | **0.901320-1.029178** | **0.928557** | 10/36 |
| P8 / always-P6 | **0.918035** | **0.867820-0.975211** | **0.929133** | 27/36 |
| always-P6 / direct | 1.064175 | 0.959444-1.160189 | 0.999380 | 8/36 |

Thus the frozen P8 dispatch policy is close to a compiler-only crossover: about 2.3% faster case-balanced, with a confidence interval crossing 1, and about 7.1% faster workload-weighted.

A post-hoc zero-incremental-telemetry diagnostic, using the measured plain source-build cost plus the frozen P8 compiler path, is `0.978428x` direct case-balanced and `0.941415x` workload-weighted. This is not a preregistered endpoint; it estimates the best case if telemetry were effectively free.

## Gate-P dispatch behavior

P8 annotated only 5/36 cases. All five annotated cases consumed a P6 fold.

- P6 beats direct source-inclusive on 7/36 cases.
- P8 annotated 3 of those 7 P6 wins.
- P8 annotated 2 cases where P6 itself was slower than direct.
- P8 bypassed 4 P6-winning cases.
- total P8 fold-consuming cases: 5
- total P8 folds consumed: 5

So the gate is conservative and avoids most annotation, but it is not yet an accurate classifier of end-to-end P6 profitability.

