A post-hoc diagnostic charging only the incremental telemetry source cost plus the P8 compiler path, relative to direct compiler cost, is `1.178966x` case-balanced and `1.123218x` workload-weighted. This isolates the remaining dispatch overhead more directly than the full source-inclusive endpoint.

## Natural EPFL control

The exact frozen ten natural evaluation cones were replayed. P8 annotated **0/10** and consumed **0 folds**. These results are therefore overhead/abstention controls, not natural-folding speed evidence.

| Comparison | Case-balanced geomean | 95% bootstrap CI | Workload-weighted | Wins |
|---|---:|---:|---:|---:|
| P8 / direct, source-inclusive | **1.032056** | **1.013398-1.051890** | **1.026753** | 2/10 |
| P8 / always-P6, source-inclusive | 0.976848 | 0.964007-0.988667 | 1.001466 | 9/10 |
| always-P6 / direct, source-inclusive | 1.056516 | 1.032874-1.082270 | 1.025250 | 0/10 |
| P8 / direct, compiler-only | 0.984667 | 0.967834-0.999729 | 1.000055 | 7/10 |

Because P8 always bypassed to direct on these cases, the apparent compiler-only difference is scheduling/noise; the executed compiler algorithm is direct. The source-inclusive 3.2% overhead is the important natural control result.

